<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Sher Khan Babi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Bahadur Khanji I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Sher Khan Babi was the founder of the princely state of Junagadh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. An officer of Pathan descent in the Mughal administration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, he declared himself independent at Junagadh in 1748 as Mughal power collapsed, taking the name Bahadur Khanji. His Babi dynasty ruled Junagadh until 1948.</p></div>
